WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have multiple jobs.
-Yes.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And yet you took
on executive producing

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
this Snoop Dogg
"Joker´s Wild" show.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
How has Snoop been
as a collaborator?

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He´s been great.
He´s been great.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.913
He watched this show with
his grandmother as a kid.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he came on
"The $100,000 Pyramid,"

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we left, and then he said,
"I want to do a show."

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m thinking,
"Okay, the guy´s been

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
hanging out with himself
too long, you know?"

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he brought up
"Joker´s Wild."

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Checked it out.
And he´s perfect.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
He loves it. He´s into it.
He has a lot of fun.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that´s really what
hosting a game show´s about,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I think
it´s a perfect fit for him.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say this,
because I´ve seen him
work with Martha Stewart.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, love that.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, he is somebody
who only does stuff he loves.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t think he would
waste time on anything else.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.943 size:75% position:38%
You´re very similar.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do "Good Morning America"
here in New York.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you also do
the Fox Sunday show.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.482
So you were in L.A. on Sunday,

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you take a red eye
every Sunday night

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.219
and come here to go to work?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You love working?

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m insane.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, honestly,
I do love working.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love --
Every job I have is great.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think because of
playing football for 15 years,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, everything now is gravy.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, like, when people go,
"Oh, it´s so hard,"

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m thinking,
"Nah, it´s not so hard."

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.272 size:81% position:41%
-Because I have looked
at all of your jobs.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
In none of them
is it legal to hit you.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.410 size:84% position:42%
And then I´m not blamed
when the team loses.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I´m not sore the next day.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is great.
-Yeah. That´s true.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you guys have a bad episode
of "Good Morning America,"

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.019
you don´t walk off and have
somebody be like, "You suck!"

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah,
that actually has happened.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.293
-But it´s about the football
stuff. It´s not a bad act.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.562
They´re like, "You didn´t throw
to local weather!"

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. But people
never forget the football.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.867
I think a lot of women know me

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
from, like, daytime TV
and all that.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don´t know
I played football.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for the guy, though --
When I was coming here,

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
I walk out of my house,
and a guy goes,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.475
"What´s up with your Giants?"

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Dude,
I haven´t played in ten years.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t know. Like..."
-Yeah, right.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Forget it, dude.
I have no control."

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:58.084
-Yeah, it´s not like there´s a
board of, like, retired players.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. We got to go to
the board of retired players

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
and say,
"What´s wrong with the team?"

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
We want them to win
just like everybody else does.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask you
about football.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously it´s been
a fraught couple of weeks

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the non-football side
of watching the games.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.967
You come from a military family.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your father was a major
in the Army. Is that correct?

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My dad is a retired major
in the Army, yeah.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:20.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, how do you feel
about the president sort of --

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
basically dividing this issue
and saying to take a knee

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
is this sort of
act of anti-patriotism?

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think that everybody
has the right to protest.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s what
this country´s about.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.986
You have rights here,
plain and simple, first of all.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.621 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
equating taking a knee

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:40.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
with patriotism
and being against soldiers

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.795
and being against the flag --
I think that the true meaning

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
of what it was
was about racial inequality.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a
totally different issue.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I see it now
as a distraction away

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
from other issues that
are going on in the world,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:55.341
from, you know -- you got North
Korea, you got Puerto Rico.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have so many other things
going on

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:00.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you take the time to pick
on football or basketball?

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.750 size:84% position:42%
I just think priorities
need to get in order

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.187
in order to do what we need to
do to make the country better.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
it does strike me that,

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
if you´re a fan in the stands,

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.961 size:88% position:44%
some fans have obviously
made the choice to boo

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.496
when players take a knee.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems, though,
within the locker room,

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
teams have had to address
something that is --

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, it´s
non-football related.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
It strikes me
that you have to --

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ideally, you´d put
all your energy towards

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
thinking about football
and thinking about the game.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.042
It also strikes me that, you
know, in a football locker room,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.110
you have a lot of white guys,
you have a lot of black guys.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think that they´ve
discussed it in a way

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s actually been
unifying for them

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
or given each other
a better understanding
of their positions?

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
And when I was playing,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had one white
defensive lineman --

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dave Tollefson.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.458
He sent all of us -- We´re on
a group text 10 years later.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
He sends us a group text,
and he said,

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I just want you guys to know
that I am with you,

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:52.098
that my kids will understand

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
everybody´s the same.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
You treat the person
for who they are,

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.670
not by the color of their skin."

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it meant a lot for us
for him to send us that.
He didn´t have to.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.141
But I think in a locker room,

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.044
when you´re going through so
much stuff outside of football,

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.546
that´s the one place you go

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
where everybody has such
an incredible understanding.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:12.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s a team. I need you,
you need me to be successful.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.387
I don´t care where you´re from

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.657
or what you do or who your --
religion, your race, anything.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re all here
for one common goal.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the locker room
is a good safe place for guys,

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that´s why you saw
so many guys come together,

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
so many teams come together
to support each other

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it is --
it´s a special place.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s very hard
to put it into words

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.840
when you haven´t been there.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
But players support each other
when the times are tough.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.145 size:84% position:42%
And Colin Kaepernick
doesn´t have a job now.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody thinks
he should have a job,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.382
but that´s up to the owners.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:45.151 size:88% position:44%
But one thing I will say
is that it takes a lot

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:48.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a guy
who´s making a lot of money,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is what everybody
seems to judge somebody by,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.924 size:78% position:39%
to put it on the line

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.061
for people who he does not know,
who he owes nothing to.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for him to say,
"Something´s not right

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I´m going to do
something about it."

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to do something
where at the end of the day,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.769
people will remember him
for that more than sports,

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is the most important
thing in the world.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I do think --
I think you´re so right.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.042 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.878 size:88% position:44%
And I think, you know --

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:14.981
We talk a lot about courage
in this country and risk.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.883
And what you said is so true.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.918
What´s getting lost in this
is Colin Kaepernick genuinely

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
did put a lot on the line.
He risked a lot.

